From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 23:05:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: lay a multi-plane image out for sharing

A video frame crosses this driver as a multi-plane image under
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR: its planes sit in one allocation, each at its own
offset, and an importer is told where they are through the image's memory
planes. This driver already lays such an image out that way and binds it that
way, but could describe only the first of them, so a two-plane frame could not
be shared at all.

A memory plane is a plane of the modifier's layout. DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR is
the only modifier offered here and lays a format's planes out in their own
order, so memory plane n is format plane n. Say that, instead of refusing
every plane past the first.

Where a plane sits was recomputed at each use, and the two computations
disagreed: the reported layout raised every earlier plane to its alignment but
not the plane being asked about, so it could name an offset below where the
bind had put it. Decide it once, when the image is created, and read it back
everywhere else.

Deciding it once also lets an importer decide it instead. A frame that arrives
as one dma-buf carries both planes in one allocation at offsets the producer
chose, and an explicit layout is how it says so - yet the layout was accepted
only when every plane repeated the offset this driver would have picked, which
for the first plane means zero and for a single-plane image means the whole
import has to start the allocation. Keep the checks that describe what Metal
can do, the row pitch it fixes and the alignment a texture may start at, and
take the offset from the layout.

Nothing in Vulkan bounds that offset, and the memory requirement is the end
of the last plane, so an offset near 2^64 wrapped the requirement below the
plane's own size and let a small allocation bind a plane far outside it. A
plane that ends past the device's largest buffer, which no allocation can
reach, is refused as an invalid plane layout.
kosmickrisp_drm_plane_offset creates such layouts on both sides of that
bound.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
